Metal Gear Solid 5 the phantom pain is  unlike any other installment in the  series Kojima Productions latest title  presents a vast open world full of  possibility and if players don't know  the basics straightforward missions can  fall apart quickly here GameSpot  presents a video guide offering 9  survival tips for any would-be  infiltrator first up dropped into the  enormous open world of Afghanistan this  time without the comfort of the series  iconic soliton sonar radars freeze mgs 5  leaves players more exposed than ever no  longer can you Scout enemies by  following dots on a viewfinder  everything now hinges on your own  in-game perception skills which means  the most important advice for all  beginners is to use your binoculars more  than any other item as soon as you  notice even the slightest hint of enemy  activity immediately equip the  binoculars by pressing r1 and locate  your target through the scope it only  takes a few seconds and once you spot an  enemy they will be permanently tagged  the benefits are significant once tagged  enemies will be outlined in red and even  if they walk out of view or stand behind  obstructions a silhouette of their  position will still be viewable from any  angle tagged enemies also appear on your  idroid map giving you a far better  understanding of your surroundings  getting into the habit of equipping  binoculars is a crucial step for  beginners but understanding how to make  the most of them is equally important  the majority of enemies who blow your  cover will be the ones you didn't tag so  it's crucial to scope out areas from a  vantage point where you can see as many  people as possible that means you're  gonna need some heights or CH initely  the plains of Afghanistan provide plenty  of areas for high altitude be at the  crest of a hill the edge of a cliff  overlooking a base or even atop one of  the enemy's own outposts never  underestimate the difference a few  meters can make even clambering onto the  rooftops of an outhouse sized prison  cell could give you just enough of an  angle to spot an enemy behind a wall be  aware of the side ups available in the  missions tab of your idroid device one  of the earliest missions available is to  capture and extract a Russian soldier  who also speaks English  Margot pledged though it's technically  an optional side quest this should be  considered a priority one operation  capturing this target alive will give  big boss and his team a Russian  interpreter without him on your side you  won't be able to interrogate and extract  information from any other Russian  soldiers with a Russian interpreter on  your team it's time to reevaluate the  rules of engagement if you spot a lone  soldier exposed and broken from the pack  tranquilizing or assassinating them is  still a viable option but even better is  capturing them in a chokehold to do that  you sneak up from behind without being  detected and hold r2 when a close range  here you can force your victim to talk  by holding a blade to their throat the  Intel you extract ranges from useful to  invaluable with intimidated guards  pointing out persons of interest or more  exotic weapons hidden away once you have  all the info you can choke enemies out  or if you'd like to indulge in your  sadistic side you can quietly stick a  blade between those  before each main mission begins malagos  solid 5 takes players to a loadout  screen where big boss can be equipped  with primary weapons and hand pistols as  well as other useful items but perhaps  just as important is the time of arrival  option which lets players fly into the  Afghanistan map at either 6 a.m. 6 p.m.  or as soon as possible without a doubt  entering a mission at dusk is the most  useful of these times granted it's not  the best way to appreciate the game  striking landscape but in the shade of  night the chances of being spotted  decrease significantly the Russian  guards line-of-sight is diminished to  the extend the big boss can sometimes  freely sprint across areas he would  usually have trouble sneaking into your  trusty diamond horse is an invaluable  companion summoned by pressing l1 and  selecting the whistle command the horse  allows you to traverse the vast plains  of Afghanistan at speed however more  surprising is how useful your steed can  be but stealth pressing the X button  when on a horseback allows big BOTS to  hang on to the horse from one side in a  way that makes it look unmanned if you  from the opposite side this can be a  particularly easy way to walk straight  past guard outposts in plane sites  without sending off an alert guards will  fix their eyes on D horse as it trots  past but few infiltration methods are as  time efficient as this one  in typical metal gear style triggering  alerts from guard will rapidly escalate  the proceedings into an all-out war  whilst going 90s Action Hero and enemies  does have its cathartic charm constantly  getting into battles will slow your  progress significantly the safest and  easiest way to avoid this is to go off  piste completely avoiding the main roads  on your way to the next objective it's  not the most scintillating option  granted but it's certainly useful if you  need to rest and decompress there are a  few things more disgracefully satisfying  in Metal Gear Solid 5 than a clean  merciless headshot however the  non-lethal approach of capturing enemies  will be far more helpful in the long  term in opening hours of the game big  boss will be given about a dozen fulton  surface-to-air recovery chutes to use in  every mission  these are baffling devices that propel  unconscious enemies to the heavens as  though they will weightless it's  quintessential Kojima logic of course  but also a quick and clean way of  capturing enemies for your mother based  as you begin to accumulate incarcerated  soldiers all of which fortunately appear  to be eager to work on mother base you  can start assigning them various duties  based on their skills open your eye draw  and go to the mother base tab and select  staff management to do this although you  probably didn't sign up to metal gear to  take part in micromanagement it can help  build up significantly the more people  you have on your R&amp;D team for example  the more weapons they can research a  manufacturer for you alternatively more  manpower in your Intel teams will give  you wider and deeper information about  Afghanistan  it is inevitable in every first  run-through of a Metal Gear game that  you will be spotted alert the guards and  trigger a manhunt on you however both  ground zeroes and a phantom pain of a  tiny grace period to dispatch enemy  guards who have spotted you this super  slo-mo reaction time is called reflex  mode and lasts about 3 seconds while the  amateur instinct is to blast away at  enemies during reflex mode panicking  like this tends to not end well  just stay calm line your crosshair on  the enemy's skull and fire just once so  there you have it our survival guide on  Metal Gear Solid 5 or the latest on the  phantom pain make sure you keep it  gangsta  you
 

